<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ntim Gyakari</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">killed 1701</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ntim Gyakari was the ruler, or Denkyirahene, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denkyira">Denkyira</a> state, which dominated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akan">Akan</a> region before the rise of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Asante</a>. He was killed in 1701 at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-feyiase">Battle of Feyiase</a>, where a coalition led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osei-tutu-i">Osei Tutu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/okomfo-anokye">Okomfo Anokye</a> defeated Denkyira. The victory freed Asante from Denkyira overlordship and launched the Ashanti Empire.</p></div>
